{
    "word": "blandishment",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                "word": "blandishment",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8dc674ea-771b-4ede-b6dc-a26e9875c830",
                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "blandishments"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Often in the plural form blandishments: a flattering speech or action designed to influence or persuade."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a74cb537-e38f-49ed-83dc-484a8924aa04",
                                "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                "text": "Thus Her with Indignation frowning, ſtern, / With Tears, and Blandiſhments Æneas ſooth’d : / She bends here Eyes averſe upon the Ground ; / And by his Speech begun is mov’d no more, / Than a hard Flint, or fix’d Marpeſian Rock."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15fc86ee-97f3-45cb-8f42-7485e6d1ba2a",
                                "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                "text": "She looked up as she heard his footsteps, and the gracious smile which her lips put on, was an invitation to make himself happy in a seat beside her. But he resisted the blandishment, and lifting his hat as he passed, with a smile in return, he soon disappeared from her presence, and joined the two who awaited him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1387a531-cae5-4ab0-a122-d599e7fd965d",
                                "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                "text": "Pat found subject and scene of his wooing unaltered, but all his specious blandishments could not induce the matured matron of 'Gi' Away Nothin' 'All' to join fortunes, though his perseverance would have delighted Bruce's spider."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cb227f8-057c-3134-b21c-746d32dbab32",
                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something alluring or attractive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "66130f40-0c9d-4a3e-8d9d-a3f4fb5b2a2a",
                                "sense_id": "1cb227f8-057c-3134-b21c-746d32dbab32",
                                "text": "We need intellectual leaders who are prepared to resist the blandishments of power and influence and who are willing to work for an ideal, however small may be the prospects of its early realization."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78aa601d-b39d-3d85-9657-2281b9f1a13c",
                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Allurement, attraction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "83fa870e-b2f8-430d-af75-96102a1cf3cb",
                        "source_entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                        "source_sense_description": "flattering speech or action designed to influence or persuade",
                        "target_lang_word": "blandice",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blandice",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ad3714b-0e25-3853-aa9f-4a89d682c370",
                                        "entry_id": "8665c8ba-b85e-328b-9a04-2cfe9419e769",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Flatterie pour gagner le cœur ou une faveur, cajolerie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33570b28-fc60-4edf-b576-ac01e2511232",
                                                "sense_id": "9ad3714b-0e25-3853-aa9f-4a89d682c370",
                                                "text": "Tes yeux aurés comme cédrat\n—Sagettes et blandice—\nClament la pompe et l’apparat\nDes vers qui, dans le Montferrat,\nChantèrent Béatrice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af9f5846-8c72-447c-b8ef-b9c100a70c6e",
                                                "sense_id": "9ad3714b-0e25-3853-aa9f-4a89d682c370",
                                                "text": "Ivre de joie, celui-ci entreprend de couvrir le financier de flagorneuses blandices, faisant valoir que ni Christophe Colomb ni Léonard de Vinci n’auraient pu réussir leur affaire sans des mécènes comme lui."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f582bab6-4181-3217-9ee3-6027948ff56e",
                                        "entry_id": "8665c8ba-b85e-328b-9a04-2cfe9419e769",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Charmes, séductions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f61b02c-595a-45a1-bcc9-a8473b6b390c",
                                                "sense_id": "f582bab6-4181-3217-9ee3-6027948ff56e",
                                                "text": "Le petit Olympe d’Issy de Michel Bouteroue est le tableau de cette cour [celle de la reine Marguerite de Valois, à Issy], à laquelle ne manqua ni la gaieté ni l’esprit : <br"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dff82e34-db64-4e8d-b0d4-b24f758cd275",
                                                "sense_id": "f582bab6-4181-3217-9ee3-6027948ff56e",
                                                "text": "Ainsi voyons-nous, mon fils, que les blandices de l'amour charnel sont plus puissantes sur les solitaires et les religieux que sur les hommes qui vivent dans le siècle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c9a49ee-8c9f-44b6-b903-cc3faff88318",
                                                "sense_id": "f582bab6-4181-3217-9ee3-6027948ff56e",
                                                "text": "[…]\nUne autre mare plus petite,\nSi l'on retourne vers le mont,\nPar l'ombre de son boys invite\nDe passer sur un petit pont,\nPour aller au lieu de délices,\nAu plus doux séjour du plaisir,\nDes mignardises, des blandices,\nDu doux repos et du loysir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47ca197a-66cf-42c9-90d4-145306ef1de9",
                                                "sense_id": "f582bab6-4181-3217-9ee3-6027948ff56e",
                                                "text": "Cependant il a vendu à son éditeur un livre intitulé Les Blandices, qui renferme, dit-il, la description de toutes les sortes d’amours. Il se flatte de s’y être montré criminel avec quelque élégance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c5057748-cc11-4982-b0b6-a6903c1cc336",
                        "source_entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
